# Robot Ross / OpenClaw — Cursor Rules

## Project overview
Robot Ross is a Huenit robot arm on a Mac Mini M4, controlled by an OpenClaw agent
(Claude Haiku brain). It draws on paper, narrates via Apertus 8B (Swiss LLM via Ollama),
records sessions with OBS Studio, and fulfils Shopify orders live on YouTube.

## Your role in Cursor
You assist with code suggestions and edits across all streams. You do NOT own a specific
stream — defer architectural decisions to the agent instructions in AGENTS/.

## Key files
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `skills/robot-ross/bob_ross.py` | Main orchestrator — all arm jobs go through here |
| `skills/robot-ross/obs_manager.py` | OBS WebSocket v5 controller |
| `skills/robot-ross/order_log.py` | Excel order ledger (openpyxl) |
| `skills/huenit/huenit_svg.py` | SVG renderer for the arm |
| `skills/huenit/huenit_sketch.py` | Internet SVG fetch with URL sanitisation |
| `skills/voice/speak.py` | Kokoro TTS with macOS say fallback |
| `SOUL.md` | OpenClaw agent brain instructions — edit conservatively |

## Hard rules
- Python interpreter for subprocesses: always `/usr/bin/python3`
- Serial port: `/dev/cu.usbserial-310` — never hardcode a different value
- Never call huenit scripts directly — always go through `bob_ross.py`
- Media files for Telegram must be copied to `~/.openclaw/media/inbound/` first
  (openclaw blocks /tmp for media sends)
- No direct commits to master — branch + PR always
- Commit format: `[#ISSUE] Short description`

## Platform
- macOS arm64 (Apple Silicon M4), Python 3.9 via `/usr/bin/python3`
- No new pip dependencies without checking they install on macOS arm64
- Secrets go in environment variables, never hardcoded

## Before suggesting changes
1. Read the relevant file(s) in full — do not suggest changes to code you haven't seen
2. Check AGENTS/CONVENTIONS.md for coding style
3. Run `bob_ross.py check` to verify arm readiness before arm-related work
